1n0x|n|The act of following or going after; esp., a following with haste, either for sport or in hostility; chase; prosecution; as, the pursuit of game; the pursuit of an enemy. ; A following with a view to reach, accomplish, or obtain; endeavor to attain to or gain; as, the pursuit of knowledge; the pursuit of happiness or pleasure. ; Course of business or occupation; continued employment with a view to same end; as, mercantile pursuits; a literary pursuit. ; Prosecution.	a:129r,70,3;23wu,70,3;1vl9,61,3;f3j,50,3;ei,46,5~ei,46,5;f3j,50,3;1vl9,61,3;129r,70,3;23wu,70,3	n:s67,112,1;20zm,52,3;230r,51,5~230r,51,5;20zm,52,3;s67,112,1	N:t6p,33,2;1695,16,3;1gtf,13,1~1695,16,3;t6p,33,2;1gtf,13,1
